  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Solar trade mission to Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Access to energy, particularly through solar power, is essential for Nigeria&#x2019;s economic development, especially in rural areas where 55% of the population lacks electricity. With high fuel costs, solar energy offers a cleaner, cheaper alternative, expanding Nigeria&#x2019;s off-grid solar market by 22% annually. Despite this growth, challenges remain, such as limited financing and fragmented market structures. A stronger local solar value chain is needed to unlock Nigeria&#x2019;s economic potential, especially for rural communities, women, and youth.To address these barriers, since early 2024, the Dutch mission in Nigeria and the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO) have collaborated on developing a solar marketplace. This platform connects key industry players, stimulates investments, and builds partnerships to promote solar energy. The solar marketplace also facilitates capacity building, positioning solar solutions, and lobbying the Nigerian government.A trade mission aims to boost awareness within the Dutch solar industry and promote business opportunities in Nigeria, particularly in off-grid solar applications for agriculture, refrigerated logistics, and infrastructure. The Nigerian market for minigrids is also expanding, offering significant revenue potential. With costs expected to decrease by over 50%, the minigrid sector could see commercial investments exceeding USD 20 billion by 2023, creating jobs and addressing Nigeria&#x2019;s energy needs. The mission seeks to capitalize on this momentum, fostering trade and development between Nigeria and the Netherlands.</narrative>
  </description>
